#17251
"Along the Wall"
"A dry and beaten bed of brown grass, long dead, recedes from growing patches

of desolate dirt.  Rising prominently from the lifeless field, a black marble

structure lies northward, wickedly grinning gargoyles encircling its ebon

roofline.  To the south, the arid plot ends abruptly at the base of the

earthen-hued stone of the walls.  East lies the corner of the outer

battlements, and west a small grove of ancient oaks.

"
