#17254
"Under an Indoor Sky"
"The destruction, so rampant throughout the rest of the compound, is barely

evident in this beautifully elegant foyer.  Grand double doors of mahogany

open to the north.  They are polished to a mirror finish and elegant in their

simplicity.  Silver-veined black marble rises to a high, vaulted ceiling, the

apex of which is lost in shadows.  Little tiny globes of light seem to pop out

of the darkness, as stars do upon the descent of night.  Constellations both

familiar and strange make themselves known in the arcing embrace of the high

ceiling.  Arches of silver mark entry to rooms to the east and west, and to

the south leads a pale carpet down an aisle, further into the building.

"
"sent 1: comma after destruction and after compound to improve readability - E

sent 6: \"familiar and unfamiliar\" is too uninteresting. \"familiar and strange/unknown/not\" would be better - E

[Soren] sure, fixed

"
