#17255
"Crushed Gravel Pathway -- Near a Pair of Towering Statues"
"Standing in the open, damp air of the massive complex, a quick glance around

provides a true perspective of the actual vastness contained within the

enclosed walls of this compound.  The crushed gravel path that winds its way

around the compound breaks in all four directions here.  The compound's

northern gate and surrounding wall are visible a short distance to the north,

and the western wall is even closer.  A pair of towering black statues stand

close by to the southeast, their craftsmanship truly exquisite.

"
""
