#17256
"Along the Wall"
"Here in the southeastern corner of the compound, walls lie to the south and

east.  Chiseled expertly into the eastern wall, a narrow stairway leads

directly to the top of the ramparts.  A creeping vine, the only life among a

field of dead or dying grass, edges its way up the staircase, its claw-like

protrusions digging into the walls for support.  Vast fields of dry, brown

vegetation stretch both to the north and westward back toward the crystalline

gates.

"
