#17258
"Along the Wall"
"Large, crisscrossing fissures riddle the earthen-colored outer wall of the

compound.  Although it appears to have taken quite a pounding at some point in

the past, the wall remains standing, its ramparts structurally sound, although

weaker, than at any other point.  A large crater has destroyed part of the

field to the west, leaving a gaping wound in the earth.  Resting within the

exact center of this deep pit lies a heavy boulder, having seemingly fallen

from the sky.

"
"[Hedrack] arrows done

