#17261
"Courtyard - Before a Guildhall"
"Great trees soar overhead, limbs outstretched but no longer clothed in

lush, green leaves.  Hazy light attempts to filter through the bare

branches, yet the courtyard still seems eternally shrouded in shadows. 

Once-fine embroidered banners hang from the tree's lower reaches, and

flutter silently in the chill wind.  The sound of sluggishly-flowing

water can be heard to the east, an almost mournful chorus.  Glimpses of

several structures can be seen through the trees in every direction, but

not so close that they disturb the courtyard.  A sturdy, wood-framed

building rises immediately to the north.

"
