#17262
"The Guildhall"
"Greasy, black stains creep out into the center of the room, as if someone

had thoughtlessly scattered the coals of the fire onto the wood of the

floor.  The stone hearth dominates the western wall of the room,

soot-stained but still intact.  An empty iron cookpot hangs from a hook

above the cold hearth, and several of the trestle tables have been

chopped into firewood-sized pieces, some stuffed into the hearth, some

scattered along the eastern side of the room.  Shattered glass litters

the bar, which is almost untouched except for several deep scratches. 

There is no evidence of the stools which must have stood before the bar,

but several of the benches have been thrown behind it.

"
