#17263
"Before a Quartz Gate"
"You stand just inside of the large gates leading from the Training Grounds

complex.  The sheer size of the southern entrance is astounding, drawing into

question how the arch and its closure were created.  A pair of crystalline

doors, a milky quartz in color, bar passage through the archway.  No hinges

can be seen in the quartz doors, though there are dark, nearly black smudges,

on the outside surface.  In the distance, less than a score of buildings rise

up from the level landscape.  Of differing designs, the structures all seem to

be of the same skillful craftsmanship.

"
