#17264
"Courtyard - Near a Temple"
"An imposing structure of obsidian marble soars upward into the empty

eastern sky.  Thinly veined with silver, the stone seems pulled from the

night sky itself.  Once-elegant arches, pillars, and flying buttresses

lie broken and shattered on the ground.  Remnants of a circular,

stained-glass window still gleam with dark, jewel tones from the center

of the facade, gaping holes diminishing its beauty.  Wickedly-grinning

gargoyles, carved from the same night-colored stone of the walls,

surround the gaping hole filled with jagged pieces of ruined glass.  An

elaborate archway carved out of a single slab of the black marble allows

entrance into the partially destroyed building.

"
