#17265
"Inside the Temple"
"Once the source of illumination for the temple's interior, tarnished

silver braziers lie toppled along the aisle, the sole upright one

attempting to light the room alone.  Dark pillars, once brilliant columns

whose silver veining reflected the flickering, brazier light, have fallen

into a sad state of neglect.  Cuts and chips mar the black marble

pillars, diminishing their value but not the memory of their beauty. 

Pews lie broken and shattered upon the floor, no longer facing the altar

at the front of the room.  In a feeble attempt to flow along the center

aisle, the tattered remnants of a dingy, white carpet converge with the

bare threads of a runner covering the raised dais in the center of the

temple.  The burnt and broken stubs of alabaster candles fill tarnished

candelabras along the outer walls of the temple.  An elaborate staircase

spirals down into darkness.

"
