#17266
"The Altar to the Gods"
"Cast shadows alternate with pools of azure radiance given off by the

blue-flamed ivory candles placed reverently up the altar.  Bent

candelabras gleam dully metallic at the edges of the room, small, grey

pools of wax filling their bowls.  The blue light reflects oddly off the

silver-inlaid runes carved into the great stone that is the altar.  Each

of the sigils, flawlessly formed of pure silver, symbolizes a god or

goddess, none taking precedence over another, or varying in anything

other than shape.  Strangely enough, the altar chamber appears

undisturbed by the destruction visited upon the remainder of the temple.

