"Guard Tower"
"Hidden from view from the grounds outside the main compound walls, a medium-

sized guard tower offers some small respite from the weather for a weary

guard.  Open on both the east and west, the tower's sole purpose appears to be

warmth and shelter for anyone on guard duty on rainy or cold nights.  A small

fire pit is set into the southern section of the wall, crafted in such as way

to allow for a flame to burn to provide warmth yet to completely hide any

light from a person standing on the ground below.  The courtyard below and to

the north is visible allowing one to see anybody entering or leaving any one

of the compound's buildings.  To the south is the small road that leads up to

the compound gates.

