was reaped upon it the rubble seems to have filled the gap partially. 

Fissures, cracks and rubble not only litter the area, but is the norm

rather than the exception here.  A large gap is evident in the wall to

the north.  No repairs have been associated with this damage yet, leaving

the only way across the gap to be a death-defying leap.  More scenes of

destruction are evident to the south, while to the north the damage seems

to have been less common.

"
"[Adakar] north is 17403, down is 17359

"
