"Cold Storage Room"
"Cold water sluggishly rolls down the southern wall of this storage room,

funneled across the room in a wooden trough.  Dimly pulsing orbs of white

light hang at equal intervals above the trough.  The water appears to be

magically moved across the room, through the trough, towards the northern

wall.  Large steel hooks, covered with coagulated blood hang from the ceiling

over the top of now rotted and broken tables.  Wooden shelves lining every

square inch of wall space are now totally bare save cobwebs and moss.  A

carved wooden ladder, slimy with mold and mildew, leads up to a large trapdoor

set into the ceiling.

