#17317
"High Mage's Room"
"The entire room seems to have every item exactly in its place.  No

battles appear to have been fought here, unlike the rest of the compound. 

A few scorch marks do mar the surface of the ivory floor, just in front

of the small fireplace midway in the northern wall.  Bookshelves abound,

covering nearly every available inch of wall space, while a desk of black

marble dominates the center of the chamber.  A glowing mage globe casts a

soft crimson light, causing the ivory surfaces to glow an evil red.  A

small archway leads out to a balcony to the west, freeing a cold breeze

to flow continually through the chamber.  An intricate rune carved

directly into the ivory door to the east, pulses a bright, majestic

magenta.

"
