#17333
"Along the Wall"
"A small hitching post huddles beneath the limbs of a spreading oak tree.  If

this tree were clothed in lush foliage, any animal tethered there would rest

comfortably in relative shade.  Unfortunately, few leaves adorn the

outstretched limbs of this old, wooden giant, nor do any appear to have

dropped recently from its branches.  A field of dried grass continues on

towards the west, approaching the corner of the compound's walls while

slightly to the southeast the front gates are visible.

"
