#17334
"Hay Loft"
"A large, square glassless window takes up the entire northern wall of the

small hayloft.  A frayed rope, used to lift hay into the loft, hangs from

a wooden beam poised just above the window.  Sections of the wooden floor

have rotted away, leaving gaping holes where the sweet smelling, freshly

cut bales once were stored.  Old, mildewy straw litters the remaining

floor, its only effective use a home for a host of insects of the most

unpleasant varieties.  A rickety plank has been placed across the largest

gap leading to the southern section of the loft, while a wooden ladder

leads back down to the stable floor.

"
"[Adakar] acode for walking across the plank of course/dex check

"
