#17335
"Marble Hallway"
"Dank and dusty, the hallway has lost the natural beauty created by the

silver-laced, obsidian marble.  The vaulted ceiling, although festooned

with cobwebs, has survived the vandalism reaped upon the rest of the

marble.  Chipped and scratched, the once-elegant arches still stand a

quiet sentinel for the rooms to the north and south.  Rusting steel

sconces, set into the western wall, hold the remains of torches that

sputtered out long ago, yet another reminder of long-term neglect.  A

spiral stair leads back up to the alcove within the temple proper, while

the hallway continues to the east.

"
