#17339
"Living Quarters"
"As if a huge explosion had ripped through here sometime in the distant

past, little remains of the room.  The once majestic dark, marble walls

have been crushed and collapsed in upon themselves, making the chamber

little bigger than a closet.  An ornate, golden shrine can still be seen

through a small crevice in the tons of rock that have fallen upon it. 

Whichever god this shrine is dedicated to is unclear, but it is obvious

that in material value it is worth a small fortune.  The only way out of

the rubble-strewn room is through the archway to the north.

"
