"Living Quarters"
"Shadows dance about the room, cast by a small tallow candle set in a

steel sconce attached to the wall.  Just below the sconce in the northern

corner of the room, resides a small shrine, covered with paintings of a

beautiful woman, and partially covered with a strange black goo.  On the

western wall, a faded tapestry hangs by mere threads, while on the

eastern wall a painting depicts a small family.  Upon the back wall

stands a mysterious rack, covered in ebony, ivory and sapphire, most of

this showing some slight damage.  A narrow bed lies under the rack,

covered in the tattered remains of a once-elegant blanket.

"
