#17342
"Entrance to Clerical Training Grounds"
"Standing as mute and blind sentinels, two towering statues flank the

human-sized, mithril door perched between them.  Despite their

lifelessness, the pair of contructs gives the strong impression of being

ever-vigilant, ever-appraising of any given situation.  No footprints are

evident in the thin layer of dust on the floor, and the chamber looks as

new as the day it was first created.  A heavily engraved archway leads

off to the south, the only accessible egress from the room.  A single

sputtering torch illuminates the room with its soft blue glow, the sconce

it rests in as shiny as the day it was created.

"
