#17343
"Living Quarters"
"A faintly glowing mage globe hovers near the central point of the vaulted

ceiling, illuminating a stunning depiction of a forest unicorn.  This

room has survived most of the vandalism that ran rampant throughout the

compound.  The marble walls are still smooth to the touch, except for a

heavily engraved section of the southern wall.  Obviously the original

inhabitant of this chamber greatly enjoyed mahogany, as both the desk and

the large bed were carved from solid pieces of this expensive wood. 

Gauging the size of the two pieces of furniture, neither seems small

enough to have fit through the northward-lying archway.  How they arrived

here is anyone's guess.

"
