"Between a Tower and the Wall"
"A dry and beaten bed of brown grass, long dead, recedes from growing

patches of desolate dirt.  Rising prominently from the lifeless field, a

seamless ivory tower lies northward, black scorch marks covering its

polished surface to a level of twenty feet.  To the south, the arid plot

ends abruptly at the base of the earthen-hued stone of the walls.  The

field of dead and drying vegetation continues on toward the east and west.

