#17346
"Mass Grave Site"
"Underfoot the loose-packed earth has been turned, the site of a hurriedly-dug,

shallow mass grave.  The ground is uneven, the mounds of dirt heaped in

roughly humanoid shapes.  A few random bones can be seen sticking out of the

ground at odd angles, exposed to view by the passage of time and weather.

Ironically there is no evidence of a fight having occurred on this spot, which

is perhaps the reason the dead were buried here.  The gravel pathway to the

north may also have been a deciding factor in the location of the burial

ground.

"
