#17347
"South of an Ancient Tree"
"Chunks of rock and fine gravel intermingle with shattered bones amongst

the trampled, dead grass underfoot.  A venerable, towering oak, its trunk

so wide ten people encircling its vast girth would be unable to touch

each other's hands, blocks further progress to the north.  Bound to the

trunk of the tree is a human skeleton, rusting iron spikes evident in

this tortured body, still skewer its wrists in place.  A short distance

to the east lies a gravel walkway, allowing easier progress than this

rubble-strewn field.

"
