#17349
"Behind the Barn"
"A narrow dirt path dead-ends at the wall of a substantial wooden barn.  The

barn is made out of a very dark, strange-looking wood.  Glancing up, a large,

paneless window set into the side of the upper level of the barn becomes

noticeable.  Hanging from a pulley attached to the roof, a rope dangles in

front of the window, probably the way occupants would haul hay to the upper

level for storage.  The path leads off to the north, running between the large

stone wall protecting the compound on the west and a thick hedgerow to the

east.

"
