#17351
"Bell Tower"
"The small tower lies at the absolute peak of the marble temple.  A golden

bell of vast girth hangs from a thick chain, nearly a handspan in

diameter, secured to one of the oaken beams that supports the domed roof. 

Set into the western wall, a lone window offers a spectacular view of the

compound's front yard.  Opposite the obsidian temple, across the

courtyard to the west and beyond a wooden building, lies the ivory tower,

quite small from here at the edge of vision.  A few cracks are set into

the marble floor, blending in nearly perfectly.

"
""
