#17353
"Crushed Gravel Pathway"
"The path here is an alley of sorts, narrowing as it cuts between the marble

structure to the east, and the wooden one to the west.  The building to the

west is built entirely of dark wood, and appears to be quite sturdy and

strong, although signs of fire damage to the building directly to the west are

apparent.  Green grasses grow at the base, and even some flowers are

noticeable, a wide contrast to the usual death and decay ever present

elsewhere in the compound.  The building of marble to the east is in a

surprisingly undamaged state, its white marble pillars showing only slight

signs of weathering.  The path continues north around to the other sides of

the two buildings, possibly to entrances.

