#17355
"Backyard"
"A row of large oak trees lines a small path in extreme disrepair to the east. 

Tall grasses have reclaimed the small area behind a dark marble building to

the north east assuming that this area was actually a path at some point in

history.  No flagstones, worked stone or the crushed gravel so evident in the

rest of the compound can be seen hiding with the grasses.  A large

statue-adorned fountain stands to the southwest, visible only because of the

bare branches of the row of oaks.  A large maple tree stands to the north

blocking passage in that direction, while the row of oaks block movement to

the south.

