#17359
"Along the Wall"
"Scorched stone, grim gray ashes and pieces of broken, burnt wood lie in

scattered disarray here.  Brushes of gray, black, and deep red paint a scene

of destruction on the surreal canvas of ground and remaining wall.  A large,

elliptical-shaped section of the wall is gone, the stone around it shattered

and charred.  Like a leopard skin, ebon spots coat the massive, defensive

structure that cowers on the ground now in pitiful heaps.  The scene of

destruction is so real, the faint scents of burning grasses and wood smoke

still linger in the air, as if it occurred only yesterday.  Amidst the

rampart's ruins, wedged between some fallen stones, a score of pikes stand

upright, their pointed barbs sharp and still intact.  The path forms a three-

way junction here, the bisected line running north and south along the wall,

the intersecting path running west along the backside of the dark marble

building.

"
"[Ilyena] Library building is NW of here

