#17364
"Along the Wall"
"In need of much repair, the cinereous and battered eastern wall looks like it

has been through hell.  The crumbled ruins fall only half as high as the

rebuilt or untouched parts of the original wall.  The curvacity of the damage

and structural arrangement of the destruction leads a person to possibly

believe magic.  In contrast to the wary eastern ruins that whisper death in a

dusty, crippled voice, to the west there lies a magnificent tree.  Appearing

to be a type of oak, it towers probably fifty feet or more easily.  Along the

wall, the path continues south for a good ways, while in the opposite

direction it follows until it hits the north wall.  The tree to the west

blocks any passage that way.

"
"[Adakar] like this room

"
