"gray stone birdbath hill"
"Small in stature, this well-crafted shallow basin rests quietly on a small

elevation nearby.  Cunningly crafted in the shape of a young girl bearing an

shallow dish of water, her face is calm and serene.  Her eyes are closed, and

her granite hair is carven so expertly it seems to have been teased into place

by the faint breeze.  A small amount of water collects in the shallow basin,

perhaps from the last rain.  Tiny grey feathers rest upon the surface of the

water, showing that this small piece, at least, was still being used as

intended.  The basin itself is too thin to fill containers from but you might

be able to lick up a little of the water to quench your thirst if necessary.

"
