#17379
"Backyard -- Columns of Pillars"
"Massive, chalk-white pillars rise proudly before you, surrounding the dark

marble building to the south.  Each pillar is easily four feet in diameter and

flawlessly crafted of pure stone.  The base of the pillars is cut into a large

cube, with a small outer ring around the column.  There are no seams in the

snowy marble, lending the impression each tree-like shaft was hewn from a

solid piece.  The night-black building can be seen through the gaps in the

pillars, the light reflecting off of the silver veins threading through the

stone.  To the northeast, a grand collanade can be seen leading towards the

grand mahogany doors of the structure.  To the west can be seen large, dark

statues, dominating the courtyard area.  The entirety of the facade lends a

serenity and peacefulness to the area, and also a sense of timelessness.

"
