named Ryxar lo'Riste at his star-day, may Cynnis prolong his life,

augment his dignity, enlighten his breast and increase his reward

twofold, because he enjoys the praise of all great men and is the

embodiment of every laudable quality.  Whoever reposes in the shadow of

his favour, his sin is transmuted to obedience and his foe into a friend.


This is how we found again our lord and master.


Every attendant and follower of our lord has an appointed duty and if, in

the performance thereof, he gives way to remissness and indolence, he is

certainly called to account and becomes subject to reproaches.

