#17398
"North of a Quartz Gate"
"You stand before a gateway carved directly into earthen-colored walls

that spread out to both the east and west.  The gate is not immense by

any standards, just allowing a person on horseback to clear the archway. 

Although not tall, the gateway is wide, allowing for the passage of large

wagons.  A pair of crystalline doors poised within the archway hang as if

by magic, as no hinges can be seen nor any other mechanical device which

could open and close these crystalline doors.  The doors are covered in

dark smudges reminescent of the after affects of great magical fires,

coupled with this are long gashes physically hacked into the quartz.

