"Along the Ramparts"
"In an odd contrast, the ramparts here appear to have seen no action in

previous battles, while to the south the wall is all but breached, with a

large chunk of it completely blown away.  Perhaps the lack of damage to

the wall is due to this segment of the wall being out of range of any war

machines which could have been moved along the road to the southeast. 

The ground outside of the wall here is fairly wide, vectoring out towards

the road, yet narrowing again towards the extreme northeastern corner of

the compound.  The roof-top roadway is blocked to the south by a gaping

hole where the wall was breached, the only way across would be a

death-defying leap, though the path to the north is still accessible.

