#17413
"Guard Tower"
"With its earthen-colored stone roof, this medium-sized guard tower was

designed for the sole purpose of comfort for a weary guard.  The tower is

open to all directions, the only reason to even call it a tower would be

the small roof, which stands a mere eight feet off of the surface of the

wall.  It was created to stand for many generations, with its four small

support pillars crafted to remain unseen from the ground below.  A small

covered firepit, overflowing with ashes, has been carved directly into

the side of the wall, allowing for a small amount of heat to radiate out

and still prevent light from giving away the position of anyone warming

themselves in this manner.

"
