"Ancient Road"
"As it winds up the mountainside, the road becomes increasingly more poorly

maintained.  Larger rocks have tumbled down from slips and partially blocked

it in several places.  Cascading down the side of the mountain are several

small, fast flowing streams.  At several points they become tiny waterfalls,

sending misty spray across the road and rocks, creating unsteady footing. 

Farther down to the east the roar of large waterfall can be heard echoing

massively off of the rocks below.  Red lichen covers the majority of rubble,

growing where even the hardy tussock cannot.

