"Living Quarters"
"While this room is far from immaculate it does appear as if it has been mostly

untouched by the damage to the rest of the temple proper.  A faintly glowing

mage globe hovers closely to the ceiling, shedding light and throwing shadows

around the room simultaneously.  The flickering of the mage globe brings the

grisly mosiac on the vaulted ceiling to life, its depiction; one of a shadow

dragon snapping its jaws shut on a fleeing vyan while at the same time

stomping its gargantuan foot down on what appears to be a young elven girl. 

An extremely large bed carved out of black oak consumes nearly the entirety of

the floor space and is the only piece of furniture remaining within this

spacious room, few other pieces of furniture could ever fit along side it.  An

obviously hand-woven rug covers nearly the entirety of the remaining black

marble floor, dark red and splotchy stains forever ruining its value.

